<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>France: Curfews issued in Paris, Nice after unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:070d4723647b148e30e90d02ef92e806505f5df695e2d723b8f206c3fdc6eeeb</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T19:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-curfews-issued-in-paris-nice-after-unrest/live-79707186--2d6d1f9bf699.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-curfews-issued-in-paris-nice-after-unrest/live-79707186?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French authorities imposed curfews in parts of several cities on Monday night after cost-of-living and anti-government protests descended into rioting and looting over the weekend. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria seeks suspects in Germany after Starlink sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0130fc93d4ffc3b8011275af658abd1a4cb9e46c3d17f553c7a04bf048ae6856</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745--e11bc2352fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Bulgarian court has issued arrest warrants for two young German nationals suspected of setting fire to Starlink antennas. The case is reminiscent of another in Poland, which Warsaw says was orchestrated by Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Emergency at Leipzig airport sparked by novice driver</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:970c51ca0e5271f35bcb07ffdd218347cc9bd5ae69b16a85bb369d00cd3f88ac</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T17:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-emergency-at-leipzig-airport-sparked-by-novice-driver/live-79695354--1d0844a30c8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-emergency-at-leipzig-airport-sparked-by-novice-driver/live-79695354?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two men breached a fence at the Leipzig/Halle airport while practicing for a driving test. Meanwhile, the "Invest in Germany Summit" is set to kick off as the government looks to fill gaps in public funding. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Cult leader guilty of murdering 190 children, 1 adult</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8dd7bafc33417b4ffb18f7dc50e801642f34055bfe5e625a8fb9d966f1486f5c</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:11:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-cult-leader-guilty-of-murdering-190-children-1-adult/a-79706279--f2f58ea97f8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-cult-leader-guilty-of-murdering-190-children-1-adult/a-79706279?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Preacher Paul Mackenzie was accused of encouraging his followers to starve themselves to death. He ran a Christian doomsday cult called the Good News International Church that claimed the end of the world was imminent.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Alberta votes on holding independence referendum</title><id>urn:rssyn